WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.880
Denmark gives Russia's defense attache seven days to leave after an alleged kill plot. This is Omni View, episode 243. After that expulsion fight, Iranian forces and Washington are still stuck on the Strait of Hormuz. A Paris court has jailed three officers for a filmed beating, and Salvadoran troops have taken their first deaths in Haiti. Then a Geneva weapons mandate, a famous maths claim, and a completed weed killer payout. A short run of other developments

00:00:29.880 --> 00:00:33.860
follows, and a look at how a shared European visa actually works.

00:00:34.930 --> 00:00:40.310
Denmark's security and intelligence service, PET, told the BBC that Russian intelligence

00:00:40.310 --> 00:00:44.470
planned and started an attempt to kill Ukrainian American near Copenhagen.

00:00:45.310 --> 00:00:48.050
Danish media name him as the rapper, Kiivstoner.

00:00:48.730 --> 00:00:50.650
His real name is Albert Vasiliev.

00:00:51.410 --> 00:00:55.170
PET says it stopped people who meant to kill him at a September concert.

00:00:55.770 --> 00:00:59.230
Three were stopped in a car near the venue on September 25th.

00:00:59.230 --> 00:01:04.710
With firearms and knives inside, two have been charged with attempted murder and with helping

00:01:04.710 --> 00:01:07.970
a foreign intelligence service, both pleaded not guilty.

00:01:08.750 --> 00:01:14.450
PET links them to loyal to familiar, a ban Danish gang it says is known for serious violent

00:01:14.450 --> 00:01:14.890
crime.

00:01:15.550 --> 00:01:21.170
Foreign Minister Lars Larky Rasmussen called the alleged attempt intimidation meant to make

00:01:21.170 --> 00:01:23.310
Denmark waver in its support for Ukraine.

00:01:23.310 --> 00:01:29.030
He wants the European Union, the block of European states, to change how Russians travel.

00:01:29.610 --> 00:01:34.430
Ashengan visa, the short-stay visa that usually lets a visitor move across much of Europe,

00:01:34.870 --> 00:01:37.050
should count only in the country that issued it.

00:01:37.510 --> 00:01:42.270
Russia's embassy called the allegations unsubstantiated and said Copenhagen produced

00:01:42.270 --> 00:01:44.310
no evidence of Moscow's involvement.

00:01:44.910 --> 00:01:49.910
Russian state media, citing the foreign ministry, say Moscow will answer the expulsion.

00:01:49.910 --> 00:01:55.370
On Saturday, European Commission President Ursula von der Leyen, head of the European

00:01:55.370 --> 00:02:00.530
Union's executive, condemned what she called an assassination attempt orchestrated by Russian

00:02:00.530 --> 00:02:04.210
intelligence, and she called it an attack on European Union soil.

00:02:04.930 --> 00:02:10.810
In July, Russia's FSB Security Service accused Vasiliev and the Ukrainian authorities of organizing

00:02:10.810 --> 00:02:14.150
a terrorist attack on military sites and personnel in Russia.

00:02:14.810 --> 00:02:16.450
He denied that on social media.

00:02:16.450 --> 00:02:21.650
France 24 reports that Danish authorities have also announced tighter limits on visas

00:02:21.650 --> 00:02:25.910
for Russian tourists, which goes further than a request still sitting with the block.

00:02:26.750 --> 00:02:31.810
Rasmussen's argument is that this was pressure on a government backing Ukraine, not a private

00:02:31.810 --> 00:02:32.270
quarrel.

00:02:32.870 --> 00:02:38.590
Armed men were stopped near a concert, tied by PET to a band gang, after Russia's own

00:02:38.590 --> 00:02:41.190
security service had already accused the performer.

00:02:41.190 --> 00:02:41.290
bomber.

00:02:41.810 --> 00:02:47.390
Vonder Lyon treats that as an attack on European Union soil and says Russia's hybrid threats,

00:02:47.650 --> 00:02:52.170
the mix of covert and open pressure, are becoming less hybrid and more real.

00:02:52.910 --> 00:02:56.490
The embassies argument is that Denmark has not shown Moscow's hand.

00:02:57.030 --> 00:03:01.670
It describes a Danish model in which a Russian trace is found and turned into a propaganda

00:03:01.670 --> 00:03:05.570
spectacle to frighten Danes and justify a long confrontation.

00:03:06.390 --> 00:03:08.690
The two people charged have pleaded not guilty.

00:03:08.690 --> 00:03:13.730
watch whether European Union governments take up the request that a Russian short-stay visa

00:03:13.730 --> 00:03:19.749
work only in the country that issued it. Iran's Islamic Revolutionary Guard Corps, a branch

00:03:19.749 --> 00:03:25.269
of its armed forces, set on Saturday that a new air defense system shot down a United States

00:03:25.269 --> 00:03:32.229
MQ-9 drone, an uncrewed military aircraft over the Strait of Hormuz. Al-Jazeera cites Iranian

00:03:32.229 --> 00:03:39.389
state broadcaster IRIB. The guard said it was the 58th US MQ-9 brought down by Iranian forces.

00:03:39.989 --> 00:03:44.489
In peacetime, one fifth of the world's oil and gas passed through that narrow sea lane.

00:03:45.109 --> 00:03:50.129
The war, launched by the United States and Israel on February 28, has killed thousands,

00:03:50.449 --> 00:03:55.889
disrupted shipping, and pushed energy prices higher. A June memorandum of understanding was never

00:03:55.889 --> 00:04:00.289
fully carried out because the two sides disagreed on freedom and security of navigation.

00:04:00.289 --> 00:04:03.569
Attacks have resumed from time to time since July.

00:04:04.029 --> 00:04:09.749
In August, the Washington Post reported that the United States had lost 45 MQ-9 drones,

00:04:10.209 --> 00:04:16.889
about 25 percent of that fleet, at a cost of more than $1.3 billion during combat operations

00:04:16.889 --> 00:04:17.489
in Iran.

00:04:18.149 --> 00:04:22.989
On Friday, the U.S. Treasury said it had sanctioned four Iranians it called oil trustees.

00:04:23.569 --> 00:04:28.569
People it says collected money from illicit oil sales to evade sanctions and a naval blockade.

00:04:28.569 --> 00:04:35.149
Among them are Muhammad Javad Bavond, a former guard intelligence officer, and Majid Taj,

00:04:35.709 --> 00:04:39.069
brother of Iranian Football Federation President Mehdi Taj.

00:04:39.889 --> 00:04:43.569
The argument turns on what must happen before ships move freely again.

00:04:44.229 --> 00:04:49.349
Foreign Minister Abbas Aragchi said seven conditions Iran sent Washington in September

00:04:49.349 --> 00:04:52.249
must be carried out before the strait reopens.

00:04:52.249 --> 00:04:57.509
Those include ending the war and lifting sanctions and the naval blockade on Iran's southern

00:04:57.509 --> 00:04:57.889
ports.

00:04:58.509 --> 00:05:03.749
He said Iran would negotiate how to implement them, that the timetable was flexible, and

00:05:03.749 --> 00:05:06.669
that talks depended on American confidence building steps.

00:05:07.169 --> 00:05:13.009
He ruled out sending the stockpile of 60% enriched uranium abroad, while saying a fair solution

00:05:13.009 --> 00:05:16.509
could be reached and that some mediator proposals were worth examining.

00:05:16.509 --> 00:05:22.349
He called the current no war, no peace state undesirable, and said Iran could not accept

00:05:22.349 --> 00:05:24.549
a deal that handed victory to the other side.

00:05:25.069 --> 00:05:30.269
At the White House, the same day, President Donald Trump said Tehran wants a deal, but

00:05:30.269 --> 00:05:31.429
not one he can accept.

00:05:32.029 --> 00:05:36.529
He said he wants a real deal, not what he called a fake deal they had been doing for 51

00:05:36.529 --> 00:05:37.069
years.

00:05:37.569 --> 00:05:40.749
He had said last week that a deal to end the war was unnecessary.

00:05:41.509 --> 00:05:46.029
Vice President JD Vance, who had blamed the war for Republicans losing both chambers

00:05:46.029 --> 00:05:50.909
of Congress this month, declined to say whether he would have authorized the February strikes

00:05:50.909 --> 00:05:55.849
to stop Iran developing a nuclear weapon. He said that call was trumps and that his

00:05:55.849 --> 00:06:01.491
job was to support the president. A Paris criminal court has convicted three police officers

00:06:01.491 --> 00:06:07.911
of intentional, racist violence in the 2020 assault of Michelle Zaclair, a black music producer,

00:06:08.471 --> 00:06:15.231
and a falsifying a police report, Al Jazeera reports. Orelian Lapperson, 29, Philippe Tondu,

00:06:15.231 --> 00:06:21.731
do, 50, and Pierre Plantier, 37, each received five years in prison, part of it suspended,

00:06:22.211 --> 00:06:23.611
and they are barred from the police.

00:06:24.291 --> 00:06:28.911
Zaclair, 47, co-founded the independent rap label Black Gold Corporation.

00:06:29.671 --> 00:06:35.511
Officers stopped him outside his Paris studio on November 21, 2020, accusing him of not

00:06:35.511 --> 00:06:39.731
wearing a face mask required under COVID rules, then pushed him inside.

00:06:39.731 --> 00:06:44.831
Over about five minutes, they punched, kicked, and used batons for some 30 blows.

00:06:45.431 --> 00:06:48.851
He suffered head trauma and a complete rupture of a biceps tendon.

00:06:49.491 --> 00:06:53.671
The presiding judge said the officers had been dishonest in their report to shield themselves,

00:06:54.151 --> 00:06:57.351
with no regard for the criminal consequences Zeckler faced.

00:06:57.991 --> 00:07:02.311
Lapperson, who filed the report, had claimed Zeckler struck out with his arms and legs.

00:07:03.051 --> 00:07:05.931
Asked if he had made that up, he told the court absolutely.

00:07:05.931 --> 00:07:11.311
He said he left the officer's blows out of the report out of fear, all three admitted

00:07:11.311 --> 00:07:12.971
excessive force and apologized.

00:07:13.611 --> 00:07:14.771
They denied racism.

00:07:15.331 --> 00:07:20.311
The judges said Zecler's account that he heard the slur sale in the gray had been consistent

00:07:20.311 --> 00:07:23.431
and that the false report damaged the officer's credibility.

00:07:24.031 --> 00:07:28.251
The New York Times reports that security cameras filmed the beating and that it set off

00:07:28.251 --> 00:07:29.331
a national backlash.

00:07:30.091 --> 00:07:35.091
Music journalist Olivier Keshen told the French paper, Sue de West, that Zecler works in

00:07:35.091 --> 00:07:37.691
the background, and is not a look at me type.

00:07:38.271 --> 00:07:41.091
Tondu said he regretted the image he had given of the police.

00:07:42.215 --> 00:07:45.655
Three Salvadoran soldiers were killed in Haiti while handling explosives.

00:07:46.375 --> 00:07:48.375
El Salvador's military set on Friday.

00:07:49.095 --> 00:07:49.975
Deutscheweller reports.

00:07:50.755 --> 00:07:55.375
These are the first officially reported deaths since a 2,000-member Salvadoran contingent

00:07:55.375 --> 00:07:56.355
was sent last month.

00:07:56.995 --> 00:08:01.215
One soldier died while being treated in the neighboring Dominican Republic, where he had

00:08:01.215 --> 00:08:02.055
been airlifted.

00:08:02.475 --> 00:08:04.395
Another was wounded and is out of danger.

00:08:04.395 --> 00:08:09.255
The military did not say where the blast happened or what explosives they were handling.

00:08:09.795 --> 00:08:15.295
President Naib Bukele sent the troops to rescue four Salvadoran Airmen, members of the United

00:08:15.295 --> 00:08:20.535
Nations backed gang suppression force, who went missing after a gang ambush on October

00:08:20.535 --> 00:08:21.935
18 in Porto Prince.

00:08:22.655 --> 00:08:27.355
Those extra troops are not part of that force, and the job has widened toward Haitian gangs.

00:08:27.975 --> 00:08:32.195
On Friday, Haiti announced an agreement with El Salvador to build three new prisons,

00:08:32.195 --> 00:08:36.775
citizens, after security and justice minister Patrick Pelicier visited El Salvador.

00:08:37.355 --> 00:08:40.255
A Salvadoran company will build them with a Haitian firm.

00:08:40.815 --> 00:08:43.215
Haitian prisons are notoriously overcrowded.

00:08:43.575 --> 00:08:47.915
In 2024, gang raids on two of the biggest freed thousands of inmates.

00:08:48.715 --> 00:08:54.555
Pelicier visited El Salvador's maximum security terrorism confinement center, known as sea

00:08:54.555 --> 00:08:59.495
caught and praised it, saying once you enter there is no hope of ever seeing the outside

00:08:59.495 --> 00:09:00.155
world again.

00:09:00.155 --> 00:09:06.395
El Salvador has imprisoned more than 90,000 people with no family visits since a state of

00:09:06.395 --> 00:09:08.175
exception began in 2022.

00:09:08.995 --> 00:09:11.815
The military extended condolences to the three families.

00:09:12.999 --> 00:09:18.699
128 countries at a United Nations conference in Geneva have agreed to elaborate a possible

00:09:18.699 --> 00:09:23.519
accord on lethal autonomous weapons over the next two years, Al Jazeera reports.

00:09:24.339 --> 00:09:28.159
These are machines that can kill without a human making the final decision to fire.

00:09:28.159 --> 00:09:32.699
The Saturday decision came under the convention on certain conventional weapons.

00:09:33.299 --> 00:09:35.719
A treaty on weapons considered especially harmful.

00:09:36.419 --> 00:09:40.079
Nearly 100 nations had pushed for swift, legally binding rules.

00:09:40.699 --> 00:09:43.699
The United States, Russia, and Israel opposed that push.

00:09:44.279 --> 00:09:46.879
The convention decides only if every member agrees.

00:09:47.519 --> 00:09:52.379
Diplomat said Russia's objections on procedure led to some formal sessions being called off,

00:09:52.779 --> 00:09:55.159
and talks on the final wording ran through the night.

00:09:55.159 --> 00:10:01.119
Swiss chair Julian Thoney said some countries rejected the word negotiate, so the text says

00:10:01.119 --> 00:10:06.539
elaboration instead. Reuters headlines the same decision as talks aimed at regulating these

00:10:06.539 --> 00:10:11.999
weapons by 2028. The states that want a ban and the states that blocked one are talking about

00:10:11.999 --> 00:10:18.379
the same machines, under a treaty that cannot move unless every member says yes. Nicole van Royen,

00:10:18.539 --> 00:10:24.819
executive director of Stop Killer Robots, a coalition of 300 organizations, told Asians France

00:10:24.819 --> 00:10:29.959
press that autonomous weapons are already in combat, including systems that use artificial

00:10:29.959 --> 00:10:35.219
intelligence to choose targets, and that delaying a binding instrument puts civilians at risk.

00:10:35.679 --> 00:10:40.039
The coalition called the mandate watered down, with no clear route to binding rules.

00:10:40.679 --> 00:10:46.099
Verity Coil, Deputy Director for Arms at Human Rights Watch, told the agency the outcome

00:10:46.099 --> 00:10:50.999
was disappointing and did not match the urgency, because the technology is racing ahead.

00:10:51.619 --> 00:10:55.659
Thoney's argument for the wording that passed is that elaborate was the verb

00:10:55.659 --> 00:11:00.019
objectives would sign, and that more than 10 years of talk still produced a

00:11:00.019 --> 00:11:04.959
step. The process can sort which weapons international humanitarian law, the

00:11:04.959 --> 00:11:09.379
rules for protecting civilians in war can ban, and which it can permit but

00:11:09.379 --> 00:11:14.219
regulate. Will the text, when it is written, name any weapon that must be banned,

00:11:14.439 --> 00:11:20.802
or only a process for talking further before 2028? Levin Alpoge, a mathematician on

00:11:20.802 --> 00:11:26.462
the technical staff of Anthropic, an Artificial Intelligence Company, says he used the company's

00:11:26.462 --> 00:11:31.342
Claude tool to produce a proof of the Riemann Hypothesis. Deutsche Vela reports,

00:11:32.042 --> 00:11:36.962
he posted the claim on his website on Friday. He believes he has, working with Claude,

00:11:37.162 --> 00:11:42.462
discovered a proof of the Riemann Hypothesis. Bernhard Riemann stated it in 1859,

00:11:43.202 --> 00:11:47.282
it is about how prime numbers, numbers divisible only by themselves and one,

00:11:47.282 --> 00:11:53.222
are spaced as they get larger. It is one of seven Millennium Prize problems chosen by the Clay

00:11:53.222 --> 00:11:59.662
Mathematics Institute, a U.S. institute that offers $1 million for a solution to each. Al

00:11:59.662 --> 00:12:05.542
Poge said the work generated more than 250,000 pages, and that he had not yet mastered all the

00:12:05.542 --> 00:12:10.922
mathematics involved. He wrote that Claude far outpaced him near the finish line. Other

00:12:10.922 --> 00:12:16.102
mathematicians still have to check the proof. Martin Britson, president of the Clay Institute,

00:12:16.102 --> 00:12:20.282
altitude, called the announcement one of historic significance in a statement quoted by the

00:12:20.282 --> 00:12:25.122
Associated Press, and said it holds the promise of a dramatic change in what people think

00:12:25.122 --> 00:12:26.502
is possible in mathematics.

00:12:27.122 --> 00:12:31.642
He also said the journey from the announcement to a place of real understanding will be long

00:12:31.642 --> 00:12:32.302
and difficult.

00:12:33.002 --> 00:12:37.922
In September, OpenAI said its technology had helped with a problem on the Navier Stokes

00:12:37.922 --> 00:12:43.182
equations, which describe how fluids such as water and air move, another of the seven

00:12:43.182 --> 00:12:44.102
prize problems.

00:12:44.102 --> 00:12:49.102
That claim also still needs independent checks, confirming the pattern would matter

00:12:49.102 --> 00:12:54.342
for a wide range of further mathematical work. Until other mathematicians sign off, it

00:12:54.342 --> 00:12:59.690
remains a claim, not a settled theorem. A completed payout is progress worth knowing

00:12:59.690 --> 00:13:04.530
for people who sued over a weed killer. A judge in Missouri has approved a settlement

00:13:04.530 --> 00:13:11.170
under which Germany's Bayer will pay up to $7.25 billion, about 6.6 billion euros,

00:13:11.170 --> 00:13:14.450
overdose, over the next two decades, Deutscheweller reports.

00:13:15.110 --> 00:13:19.310
The cases come from people who say they should have been warned that Roundup could cause

00:13:19.310 --> 00:13:20.710
non-Hodgkin lymphoma.

00:13:21.450 --> 00:13:22.850
The deal applies nationwide.

00:13:23.550 --> 00:13:27.810
People already ill and people who develop the cancer later could receive an average of

00:13:27.810 --> 00:13:33.330
between $10,000 and $165,000, depending on how they use the product.

00:13:33.850 --> 00:13:36.990
Their age at diagnosis and how severe the illness is.

00:13:36.990 --> 00:13:40.910
Deutsche Wella reports that some lawyers say the payments are too low.

00:13:41.290 --> 00:13:42.910
The decision could be appealed.

